#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""nvcc_emu: nvcc drop-in that builds sm_90a CUDA code into sm_80 binaries (PLAN section 3).

Flow:
  1. Architecture options (-arch/-code/-gencode and long forms) are replaced by the single
     ``-gencode=arch=compute_<A>,code=sm_<A>`` (A from WGEMU_SRC_ARCH, default 90a).
  2. ``<real nvcc> -dryrun -keep -keep-dir <dir> <args>`` lists the compilation steps; the
     ``#$ NAME=value`` lines are exported, the other ``#$`` lines are run one by one.
  3. Every PTX written by cicc for compute_86+ is translated in place with ptxemu (the
     emulation library PTX is merged right after the module header, ``.target`` becomes sm_80).
     PTX files given as inputs are translated into the keep directory before ptxas reads them.
  4. ptxas / nvlink ``sm_9x`` -> ``sm_80``; fatbinary ``--image3=kind=elf,sm=90a`` -> ``sm=80``;
     PTX images (kind=ptx) are dropped.

Environment:
  WGEMU_DISABLE=1        run the real nvcc unchanged
  WGEMU_MODE             exact (default) | fast | check
  WGEMU_SRC_ARCH         90a (default) | 90
  WGEMU_TRAP=1           check mode: trap on violations
  WGEMU_ALLOW_CLUSTER=1  drop .reqnctapercluster > 1 instead of failing
  WGEMU_ASYNC_DELAY=1    E1: asynchronous copies into shared memory (cp.async.bulk global->shared,
                         cp.async.bulk.tensor loads, cp.async) write poison at issue; the data
                         arrives when a thread observes the completion (mbarrier test_wait /
                         try_wait success, cp.async.wait_group / wait_all). Violations print
                         WGEMU-VIOLATION async-delay-* (tools/ptxemu/instrument.py)
  WGEMU_DL_SLOTS         E1 pool slots per module (default 128: CTAs running at the same time)
  WGEMU_DL_RECORDS       E1 pending copies per CTA (default 4096)
  WGEMU_COUNT=1          E2: per-launch counters; host/shim.c prints one WGEMU-COUNT line per
                         launch of a counted kernel
  WGEMU_REAL_NVCC        real nvcc path (default: CUDA home recorded by make_cuda_home_shadow.sh,
                         then $CUDA_HOME/bin/nvcc, then /usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc)
  WGEMU_LIB              use this emu_lib.ptx instead of building runtime/emu_lib.cu
  WGEMU_CACHE_DIR        emu_lib.ptx cache (default ~/.cache/wgemu)
  WGEMU_INVENTORY        inventory.tsv for the remaining-opcode check
  WGEMU_KEEP=1           keep all intermediate files

Extra option (removed before calling nvcc):
  --wgemu-shadow <relpath>:<regex>:<replacement>
      Copy the header <relpath> (found through -I / -isystem) into <keep>/wgemu_shadow with
      re.subn(regex, replacement, text, flags=re.M) applied (at least one match required) and
      put that directory first on the include path. ':' inside the fields is written '\\:'.

The translation report (<stem>.wgemu_report.json), the remaining sm_86+ check
(<stem>.wgemu_check.txt), the original PTX (<stem>.wgemu_orig.ptx) and the command list
(wgemu_cmds.sh) stay in the keep directory: -keep-dir if given, otherwise <output>.wgemu.d.
"""

